      "moduleId": "rn_7Tgb4gzybkSVcPDf::L3",
      "stem": "Explain why the compound's own combustion value enters the sum with a reversed effect.",
      "misconceptionClass": "sign geometry",
      "kind": "explain-why",
      "modelAnswer": "Formation climbs from elements up to the compound while combustion descends from it, so the compound's leg runs opposite to the cycle's direction and its tabulated value enters effectively flipped.",
